+[Download full CV (PDF)](../files/MariaPaolaVaccaro_CV.pdf){: .btn .btn--primary}
+
+---
+
+## Research profile
+
+I am a computational astrophysicist and PhD candidate at Heidelberg University (supervisor: Prof. Michela Mapelli), modelling how black holes grow from stellar to intermediate and supermassive masses, and what their gravitational-wave mergers reveal about the early Universe. I showed that AGN disks can grow black holes through the pair-instability gap into the intermediate-mass range, but only in low-viscosity disks with efficient gas hardening, and that the resulting populations match systems like GW190521 and GW231123. Expected defence January 2028; available for postdoc and fellowship positions from late 2027.
+
+---
+
+## Education
+
+**PhD in Astronomy and Cosmic Physics** (Sep 2023 – 2028, expected)
+Institute for Theoretical Astrophysics (ITA/ZAH), Heidelberg University, Germany.
+Supervisor: Prof. Michela Mapelli. Thesis: *"Binary Black Hole population in the Local Universe"*
+Funded by ERC Consolidator Grant DEMOBLACK and the Heidelberg Cluster of Excellence STRUCTURES.
+
+**MSc in Astrophysics and Cosmology** (Oct 2020 – Sep 2022)
+Università degli Studi di Padova, Italy. Grade: 110/110 cum laude (GPA: 29.4/30).
+Thesis: *"Hierarchical Black Hole Mergers in Active Galactic Nuclei"*
+
+**BSc in Physics** (Sep 2016 – Sep 2019)
+Università di Pisa, Italy. Grade: 110/110 cum laude (GPA: 28.6/30).
+
+---
+
+## Selected highlights
+
+- **10 papers**, of which 4 as first author. ~80 citations on first-author papers. h-index 7 (NASA ADS, Sept. 2026)
+- **12 conference contributions** (EAS, MODEST, ET Symposium, among others) and seminars at ISTA Vienna, GSSI L'Aquila, University of Arizona, and UNAB Santiago
+- **Invited** to write a contribution for a Royal Society theme issue (2025) and to give talks at the Niels Bohr Institute (2024) and the Physics of Data Workshop, Venice (2023)
+- **SSC Fellowship** (2026–27) in research software engineering, Scientific Software Center, Heidelberg; PhD fellow of IMPRS; member of the STRUCTURES Young Research Convent
+- **Mentoring and service:** co-supervised 3 students (1 MSc, 2 BSc); teaching assistant for 2 semesters; referee for A&A, JCAP, and PRD; member of the Einstein Telescope collaboration (OSB Div. 3)
+
+---
+
+## Methods and software
+
+**Modelling:** semi-analytic frameworks, population synthesis, SPH hydrodynamical simulations, Bayesian statistics
+
+**Languages:** Python, C/C++, CUDA, Fortran
+
+**HPC:** MPI, Slurm, GPU and cluster workflows (EuroHPC summer school, RIKEN; SSC research-software fellow)
+
+**Code:** lead developer of [FastClusterAGN](https://gitlab.com/mariapaola.vaccaro/fastcluster_agn) and [ARISE](https://gitlab.com/mariapaola.vaccaro/arise)
+
+---
+
+## Representative publications
+
+* [Cosmic merger rates and population evolution of binary black hole mergers in AGN disks](https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.40787) — Vaccaro et al., submitted (2026)
+* [Black hole populations and hierarchical growth across the AGN parameter space](https://www.aanda.org/articles/aa/full_html/2026/04/aa56761-25/aa56761-25.html) — Vaccaro et al., A&A 714, A322 (2026)
+* [The role of migration traps in the formation of binary black holes in AGN disks](https://doi.org/10.1051/0004-6361/202556761) — Vaccaro et al., A&A 708, A171 (2026)
+* [Impact of gas hardening on hierarchical black hole mergers in AGN disks](https://www.aanda.org/articles/aa/full_html/2024/05/aa48509-23/aa48509-23.html) — Vaccaro et al., A&A 685, A51 (2024)
+
+[Full publication list on ADS](https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/search/q=author%3A%22Vaccaro%2C+M.+P.%22&sort=date+desc){: .btn}
